{"title":"Planned improvements to the car","markdown":{"headingText":"Planned improvements to the car","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n## Mechanical changes to car (by priority):\n\n- Modify steering and front brakes to reduce knocking\n\n  - Make sure the steering column is locked with C clips and cannot be accidentally disassembled\n\n- Remake suspension plates to remove camber from wheels\n\n  - Make sure the wheels are correctly pressurized\n\n  - Camber adjustability would be good\n\n- Move windshield hinge to front of windshield (makes entering/dismounting easier)\n\n  - Or a 4-bar linkage\n\n- Improve brake ergonomics\n\n  - Improve cable routing under the upper floor and also out the sides so that it doesn't pull on floor and side panels\n\n  - Bleed rear brakes\n\n  - Actual brake pedal\n\n- Remake front brake caliper mounts to fit\n\n  - Some level of adjustability would be good\n\n- Remove front and/or rear suspension to reduce weight (if rules permit)\n\n  - Redesign suspension with shorter, softer springs\n\n- **Standardize one or two screw sizes so we don't have to spend forever looking for the right bits**\n\n- Improve driver comfort (how?)\n\n  - Mount steering, pedals, harness, buttons, seat, etc. around the driver\n\n  - Better seat (hammock seat was pretty cool)\n\n- Removable side panels would be nice to make serviceability easier\n\n- Fix the floor\n\n- If necessary, improve airflow in fuel cell area with more strategic scoops/vent holes\n\n## Changes to electrical system (by priority):\n\n- Identify and fix cause of power shutoffby\n\n- Replace existing motor with more powerful motor\n\n- Better cable routing\n\n## Changes to fuel cell system (by priority):\n\n- Make the back panel that all the plumbing is mounted to easier to remove\n\n- Figure out the correct tank dimensions\n\n- Pay attention to conical vs cylindrical threading\n\n# Logistical changes for next year\n\n## Updated packing list\n\n- 3D printer and filament!\n\n## Stuff to buy\n\nNew helmet\n\nNew regulator\n\nL connectors for fuel cell\n\nLower level gas can\n\nMore drills\n\nComplete sets of tools\n\nMore sharpie colors\n\nMore wire\n\nMore swagelock tube bending tools\n\nPTFE tubing\n\nThe right brake fluid\n\nRolling chassis table\n\nTool chest/pack out\n\nNew motor\n\nC clips\n\nChairs\n\n## General Advice\n\nLabel stuff\n\nLearn how to mount stuff on tubes\n\nLearn how to tolerance 3D prints\n\nGet sponsors\n\nRead the whole rule book\n\nGet more camping chairs\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","output-file":"2026 Shell Eco Marathon Debrief Document.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of content